, London: […] A[ndrew] Millar, and sold by Thomas Cadell, […], published 1768, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A geometrid moth of the species Orthonama obstipata.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(computing) A package containing programs or libraries for the Ruby programming language.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(uncountable, printing, uncommon, obsolete) A size of type between brilliant (4-point) and diamond (4½-point), running 222 lines to the foot.", "tags": ["obsolete", "uncommon", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(baseball) A strong, dominating pitching performance.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["2025, Associated Press, Crochet gets 1st career shutout and complete game as Red Sox beat Rays for 9th straight win by Associated Press,\nHe didn’t walk a batter in his 100-pitch gem"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(Internet slang) Internet content of good quality.", "tags": ["Internet", "countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["coal", "brimstone"], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["gemstone", "jewel", "precious stone"], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/d͡ʒɛm/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/d͡ʒɪm/", "tags": ["pin pen merger"]}], "forms": [{"word": "gems", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "gemming", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "gemmed", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "gemmed", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(transitive) To adorn with, or as if with, gems.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "[T]he fair star / That gems the glittering coronet of morn, / Sheds not a light so mild, so powerful, / As that which, bursting from the Fairy's form, / Spread a purpureal halo round the scene, / Yet with an undulating motion, / Swayed to her outline gracefully.", "reference": "1813, Percy Bysshe Shelley, “Canto I”, in Queen Mab; […], London: […] P. B. Shelley, […], →OCLC, page 6:"}, {"text": "A few bright and beautiful stars gemmed the wide concave of heaven[…].", "reference": "1827, Various, The Mirror of Literature, Amusement, and Instruction, Vol. 10,:"}, {"text": "Above was the firmament, gemmed with worlds, and sublime in immensity.", "reference": "1872, J. Fenimore Cooper, The Bravo:"}, {"text": "The rain Shook from fruit bushes in new showers again As I brushed past, and gemmed the window pane.", "reference": "1920, John Freeman, Poems New and Old:"}, {"text": "And those salt tears your lashes gemmed / Were but the breath of flame distilled; / Flame white and pure, and diademmed / With suffering,—pain with joy fulfilled.", "reference": "1922 February, Miriam Campbell, “A Dream of Brittany”, in The Educational Times: A Review of Ideas and Methods, volume IV (new series)/LXXIV (old series), page 64, column 1:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["begem"], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gem", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}